
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E G : Points
AB ⟂ AC [00]
B,C,D are collinear [01]
AD ⟂ BC [02]
C,E,A are collinear [03]
∠EBA = ∠CBE [04]
B,E,G are collinear [05]
G,A,D are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. C,E,A are collinear [03] & B,D,C are collinear [01] & G,D,A are collinear [06] & AD ⟂ BC [02] & AB ⟂ AC [00] ⇒  ∠EAB = ∠BDG [07]
002. B,D,C are collinear [01] & B,E,G are collinear [05] & ∠EBA = ∠CBE [04] ⇒  ∠EBA = ∠DBG [08]
003. ∠EAB = ∠BDG [07] & ∠EBA = ∠DBG [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ∠AEB = ∠BGD [09]
004. C,E,A are collinear [03] & B,E,G are collinear [05] & G,A,D are collinear [06] & ∠AEB = ∠BGD [09] ⇒  ∠AEG = ∠EGA [10]
005. ∠AEG = ∠EGA [10] ⇒  AE = AG
==========================
